There are three types of CSS
i) inline CSS: This css is written in the HTMl document under a specific HTML element to which the CSS applies. Under the html opening tag CSS can be written using
the style attribute. 
<h1 style="font-size=20px; color=blue;"> Hello World </h1>

ii) internal CSS: This type of CSS is written within the HTML document under the <head> and </head> tags using the <style> tag. 
<head>
  <style>
    h2{
      font-size: large;
      color: blue;
    }
  </style>
</head>

iii) external CSS: This type of CSS is written in a separate css file, then this file is linked to the HTMl file using <link> tag. 
styles.css
   h2{
      font-size: large;
      color: blue;
    }

Specificity: inline CSS is carry more prescedence while the internal and external carry same. 

Which CSS should be used?
External CSS should be used more commonly because,
> Inline CSS and Internal CSS makes the HTML code look complex reducing the readability and maintainability. 
> Extenral CSS separated the different files on the basic of their purposes and helps in achieving separation of concerns. It keeps the HTML file separated for
  defining the structure and CSS file for styling of the web pages.
